00:40:54.350 --> 00:40:56.120
And I'll just click Create.

00:40:56.120 --> 00:40:59.870
And so just like before with
Cloud Run fully managed,

00:40:59.870 --> 00:41:03.530
now Cloud Run on GKE is
deploying the service,

00:41:03.530 --> 00:41:07.020
bringing in the container,
creating a URL for me,

00:41:07.020 --> 00:41:08.672
and making everything work.

00:41:08.672 --> 00:41:10.130
And so now this is
actually running

00:41:10.130 --> 00:41:11.785
on my Kubernetes instance.

00:41:11.785 --> 00:41:13.160
So if I click on
this URL, you'll

00:41:13.160 --> 00:41:14.493
see here's the same application.

00:41:14.493 --> 00:41:16.910
It says running on
Cloud Run on GKE,

00:41:16.910 --> 00:41:18.970
just in case you
didn't believe me.

00:41:18.970 --> 00:41:20.690
And then we can switch
back and actually

00:41:20.690 --> 00:41:26.180
look at the Kubernetes UI.

00:41:26.180 --> 00:41:28.140
And I'll show you again.

00:41:28.140 --> 00:41:30.740
If we go to workloads,
for example,

00:41:30.740 --> 00:41:33.920
you can see down here the
PDF service has been deployed

00:41:33.920 --> 00:41:35.920
onto this Kubernetes cluster.

00:41:35.920 --> 00:41:37.612
And if I switch
over to services--

00:41:37.612 --> 00:41:40.070
and for those of you who are
unfamiliar in Kubernetes land,

00:41:40.070 --> 00:41:44.343
services are about networking,
not about services--

00:41:44.343 --> 00:41:46.760
you'll see the PDF service
here with both an external name

00:41:46.760 --> 00:41:48.330
and a cluster IP address.

00:41:48.330 --> 00:41:51.740
So this service that I created,
or that Steren created earlier

00:41:51.740 --> 00:41:53.810
is now running inside
my Kubernetes cluster

00:41:53.810 --> 00:41:57.920
using the same API, the same
UI, the same experience.

00:41:57.920 --> 00:41:59.850
I didn't have to
change anything.

00:41:59.850 --> 00:42:02.090
But I could easily
deploy it into Kubernetes

00:42:02.090 --> 00:42:04.467
or into manage serverless.

00:42:04.467 --> 00:42:06.050
If we could switch
back to the slides.

00:42:10.030 --> 00:42:10.970
Thanks.

00:42:10.970 --> 00:42:13.130
So we have shared tooling.

00:42:13.130 --> 00:42:14.087
We also have a CLI.

00:42:14.087 --> 00:42:16.670
Instead of specifying the region
that you want to deploy into,

00:42:16.670 --> 00:42:19.400
you specify the cluster name
that you want to deploy.

00:42:19.400 --> 00:42:20.570
It's very simple.

00:42:20.570 --> 00:42:22.133
But how do we do all this?

00:42:22.133 --> 00:42:24.300
We could have done it in a
number of different ways.

00:42:24.300 --> 00:42:27.440
But we did this based on
the Knative Project, which

00:42:27.440 --> 00:42:30.650
is an open source project
for serverless building

00:42:30.650 --> 00:42:34.010
blocks on Kubernetes that we
launched last year at Next,

00:42:34.010 --> 00:42:35.190
about eight months ago.

00:42:35.190 --> 00:42:38.720
And it provides the common API,
the common runtime contract,

00:42:38.720 --> 00:42:42.890
and a reference implementation
for how to do everything

00:42:42.890 --> 00:42:44.570
that we've shown here today.

00:42:44.570 --> 00:42:46.130
It implements
learnings from Google

00:42:46.130 --> 00:42:47.840
and has more than 50
different companies

00:42:47.840 --> 00:42:50.280
who have contributed
into the project.

00:42:50.280 --> 00:42:53.720
So it's really taking
this standard approach

00:42:53.720 --> 00:42:56.690
to how to run services
workloads on top of Kubernetes.

00:42:56.690 --> 00:42:58.850
And it provides this
portable experience

00:42:58.850 --> 00:43:02.870
between both of the managed
services that we offer on GCP,

00:43:02.870 --> 00:43:05.630
as well as being able to take it
anywhere that Kubernetes runs.

00:43:05.630 --> 00:43:09.110
You can deploy Knative onto
that Kubernetes cluster

00:43:09.110 --> 00:43:12.380
and have the same tooling,
the same API, and everything

00:43:12.380 --> 00:43:13.480
working there.

00:43:13.480 --> 00:43:15.380
In fact, at the developer
keynote tomorrow

00:43:15.380 --> 00:43:17.270
night, Steren and
I will show you

00:43:17.270 --> 00:43:20.210
how we can even deploy that
onto an IBM cluster running

00:43:20.210 --> 00:43:23.750
Manage Knative that really
emphasizes that portability.

00:43:23.750 --> 00:43:26.840
And you can learn more
by going to knative.dev.

00:43:26.840 --> 00:43:30.490
[MUSIC PLAYING]

